      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/writerryan/{size}/2710_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-08-23T14:29:36.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For the last Kickstarter, I got an email notification with a tracking number, which I obsessed over for a full week before receiving my package.&nbsp; Maddeningly, I could see that my package had been received at the St. Louis shipping center and then sat there for days and days while they held it to make sure it didn't arrive to me earlier than they'd promised. :(I think you've asked the question is exactly the right place.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I have two friends who have worked for UPS at the sort facilities, and they've been there at the same time as packages that were pending delivery for them but weren't allowed to take them home and had to wait until at least the next day.  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/confused.png?v=12\" title=\":confused:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":confused:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
